<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Modified <math id="A2.SS3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> contraction and proof of the main theorem</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We now prove <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 3.5 (𝜒^2 convergence). ‣ 3.3 Ideal Proximal BPS ‣ 3 The Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a> using a discrete modified <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>
argument. For <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in L_{0}^{2}(\pi_{\eta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in L_{0}^{2}(\pi_{\eta})</annotation></semantics></math>, write</p>
<table id="A2.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathsf{P}}\coloneqq\mathsf{P}f\,,\hskip 20.00003ptf_{\perp}\coloneqq\mathsf{P}^{\perp}f\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathsf{P}}\coloneqq\mathsf{P}f\,,\hskip 20.00003ptf_{\perp}\coloneqq\mathsf{P}^{\perp}f\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math> are, respectively, the macroscopic
and microscopic parts of <math id="A2.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Fix <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\rho\leq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\rho\leq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>. The ordinary <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> energy does not by itself give
the required one-step contraction. Indeed, since <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}</annotation></semantics></math> is unitary and
<math id="A2.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}</annotation></semantics></math> is a contraction,</p>
<table id="A2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\mathsf{K}f\|^{2}-\|f\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\mathsf{K}f\|^{2}-\|f\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=(1-\rho)^{2}\,\|\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}f_{\perp}\|^{2}-\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=(1-\rho)^{2}\,\|\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}f_{\perp}\|^{2}-\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq-\rho\,(2-\rho)\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\leq-\rho\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.150em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq-\rho\,(2-\rho)\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\leq-\rho\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p">This estimate controls <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math> but gives nothing when
<math id="A2.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=f_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=f_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Reflection moves part of <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> into the
microscopic subspace, but this transfer is not captured by the <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> norm,
which is a standard difficulty in hypocoercivity. The modified <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>
method addresses this difficulty by adding a corrector to the Lyapunov
function. The corrector records the transfer from <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> to
<math id="A2.SS3.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math>, allowing the contraction in
(<a href="#A2.E18" title="Equation B.18 ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.18</span></a>) to also control <math id="A2.SS3.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This idea goes back to Dolbeault, Mouhot, and Schmeiser <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>; here we
follow the refinement of Fan, Li, and
Lu <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To construct the corrector, we first isolate the part of <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math> that
couples to <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> under reflection. Define</p>
<table id="A2.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathsf{V}}\coloneqq\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}f_{\perp}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathsf{V}}\coloneqq\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}f_{\perp}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p3.2" class="ltx_p">By (<a href="#A2.E16" title="Equation B.16 ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.16</span></a>),
<math id="A2.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}f_{\perp}=\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}f_{\perp}=\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{V}}</annotation></semantics></math>, while the component of
<math id="A2.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math> orthogonal to <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{ran}(\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ran</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{ran}(\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}})</annotation></semantics></math> is annihilated by
<math id="A2.SS3.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> is an isometry,
<math id="A2.SS3.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{V}}=\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}f_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{V}}=\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}f_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math> is the orthogonal
projection of <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math> onto <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{ran}(\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ran</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{ran}(\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}})</annotation></semantics></math>, and hence
<math id="A2.SS3.p3.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|\leq\|f_{\perp}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|\leq\|f_{\perp}\|</annotation></semantics></math>. We work with <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathsf{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathsf{V}}</annotation></semantics></math>, rather
than with this projection itself, because <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathsf{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathsf{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS3.p3.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> both belong to <math id="A2.SS3.p3.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}</annotation></semantics></math> and can therefore be
paired in the corrector.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p">With this notation, let <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> be a weight to be chosen below and
define the modified Lyapunov function</p>
<table id="A2.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(f)\coloneqq\|f\|^{2}+\omega\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℒ</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(f)\coloneqq\|f\|^{2}+\omega\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.2" class="ltx_p">where the corrector is</p>
<table id="A2.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})\coloneqq\frac{1}{2}\,\bigl(\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}-\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}\bigr)-\bigl\langle\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}}\bigr\rangle\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})\coloneqq\frac{1}{2}\,\bigl(\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}-\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}\bigr)-\bigl\langle\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}}\bigr\rangle\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p4.3" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is applied only on <math id="A2.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}</annotation></semantics></math>, where
<math id="A2.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\succeq\gamma_{\rm gap}I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\succeq\gamma_{\rm gap}I</annotation></semantics></math>, so the corrector is well-defined.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p">To motivate this choice, recall from (<a href="#A2.E7" title="Equation B.7 ‣ B.1 Operator framework and micro–macro decomposition ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.7</span></a>) that
<math id="A2.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{K}</annotation></semantics></math> acts in two stages: it first maps</p>
<table id="A2.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathsf{P}}+f_{\perp}\longmapsto f_{\mathsf{P}}+(1-\rho)\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}f_{\perp}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathsf{P}}+f_{\perp}\longmapsto f_{\mathsf{P}}+(1-\rho)\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}f_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.2" class="ltx_p">and then applies <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}</annotation></semantics></math>. For the moment, set <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho=0</annotation></semantics></math> and replace
<math id="A2.SS3.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}</annotation></semantics></math> by <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-I_{\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-I_{\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The error
<math id="A2.SS3.p5.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}</annotation></semantics></math> introduced by this replacement is controlled by
<a href="#A2.Thmtheorem2" title="Proposition B.2 (Global half-turn bound). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>. Denote the resulting idealized operator
by</p>
<table id="A2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{K}_{\rm id}\coloneqq\mathsf{U}(\mathsf{P}-\mathsf{P}^{\perp})\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mi>id</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>𝖴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{K}_{\rm id}\coloneqq\mathsf{U}(\mathsf{P}-\mathsf{P}^{\perp})\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.3" class="ltx_p">Set <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\coloneqq\mathsf{K}_{\rm id}f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mi>id</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\coloneqq\mathsf{K}_{\rm id}f</annotation></semantics></math>, and define the corresponding components by</p>
<table id="A2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\mathsf{P}}\coloneqq\mathsf{P}g\,,\hskip 20.00003ptg_{\mathsf{V}}\coloneqq\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{P}^{\perp}g\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\mathsf{P}}\coloneqq\mathsf{P}g\,,\hskip 20.00003ptg_{\mathsf{V}}\coloneqq\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{P}^{\perp}g\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.4" class="ltx_p">In terms of these components, <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{K}_{\rm id}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mi>id</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{K}_{\rm id}</annotation></semantics></math> is represented by the
operator-valued rotation matrix</p>
<table id="A2.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{pmatrix}g_{\mathsf{P}}\\
g_{\mathsf{V}}\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}&amp;-\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\\
\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}&amp;\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\end{pmatrix}\begin{pmatrix}f_{\mathsf{P}}\\
f_{\mathsf{V}}\end{pmatrix}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{pmatrix}g_{\mathsf{P}}\\
g_{\mathsf{V}}\end{pmatrix}=\begin{pmatrix}\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}&amp;-\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\\
\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}&amp;\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\end{pmatrix}\begin{pmatrix}f_{\mathsf{P}}\\
f_{\mathsf{V}}\end{pmatrix}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.5" class="ltx_p">Indeed, the first component follows immediately from the block representation
of <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}</annotation></semantics></math> and the polar decomposition
(<a href="#A2.E16" title="Equation B.16 ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.16</span></a>):</p>
<table id="A2.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathsf{P}\mathsf{U}(f_{\mathsf{P}}-f_{\perp})=\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{P}}-\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}f_{\perp}=\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{P}}-\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}f_{\perp}=\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{P}}-\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{V}}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖯𝖴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathsf{P}\mathsf{U}(f_{\mathsf{P}}-f_{\perp})=\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{P}}-\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}f_{\perp}=\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{P}}-\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}f_{\perp}=\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{P}}-\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{V}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.6" class="ltx_p">For the second component, substitute
<math id="A2.SS3.p5.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}=\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}=\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> into
<math id="A2.SS3.p5.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\perp}=-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\perp}=-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> from
(<a href="#A2.E5" title="Equation B.5 ‣ B.1 Operator framework and micro–macro decomposition ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>). Since <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> commutes with
<math id="A2.SS3.p5.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>, this gives</p>
<table id="A2.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\perp}=-\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\perp}=-\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.7" class="ltx_p">The ranges of <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\perp}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS3.p5.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> lie in <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}</annotation></semantics></math>, where
<math id="A2.SS3.p5.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded. Applying <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> to the
displayed identity therefore gives
<math id="A2.SS3.p5.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\perp}=-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\perp}=-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence</p>
<table id="A2.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle g_{\mathsf{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle g_{\mathsf{V}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex15.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{P}^{\perp}\mathsf{U}(f_{\mathsf{P}}-f_{\perp})=\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}(\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{P}}-\mathsf{U}_{\perp\perp}f_{\perp})=\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{P}}+\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}f_{\perp}=\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{P}}+\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{V}}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝖴</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{P}^{\perp}\mathsf{U}(f_{\mathsf{P}}-f_{\perp})=\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}(\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{P}}-\mathsf{U}_{\perp\perp}f_{\perp})=\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{P}}+\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}f_{\perp}=\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{P}}+\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{V}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.8" class="ltx_p">This proves the claimed matrix formula. Since
<math id="A2.SS3.p5.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2}+\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{2}=I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2}+\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{2}=I</annotation></semantics></math>, the block matrix acts as a rotation on
<math id="A2.SS3.p5.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}\oplus\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><mo>⊕</mo><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}\oplus\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Under this rotation,
direct substitution into (<a href="#A2.E20" title="Equation B.20 ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.20</span></a>) gives</p>
<table id="A2.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathscr{C}(g_{\mathsf{P}},g_{\mathsf{V}})-\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathscr{C}(g_{\mathsf{P}},g_{\mathsf{V}})-\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 10.00002pt=\mathscr{C}(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{P}}-\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{V}}\,,\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{P}}+\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{V}})-\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="1.278em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 10.00002pt=\mathscr{C}(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{P}}-\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{V}}\,,\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{P}}+\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}f_{\mathsf{V}})-\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E21"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 10.00002pt=-\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="1.278em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 10.00002pt=-\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.9" class="ltx_p">For <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\omega&lt;\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\omega&lt;\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, combining the leading terms from
(<a href="#A2.E18" title="Equation B.18 ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.18</span></a>) and
(<a href="#A2.E21" title="Equation B.21 ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.21</span></a>), and using
<math id="A2.SS3.p5.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|\leq\|f_{\perp}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|\leq\|f_{\perp}\|</annotation></semantics></math>, gives</p>
<table id="A2.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\rho\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}+\omega\,\bigl(-\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}\bigr)\leq-\omega\,\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}-(\rho-\omega)\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0.150em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>ω</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\rho\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}+\omega\,\bigl(-\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}\bigr)\leq-\omega\,\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}-(\rho-\omega)\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p5.10" class="ltx_p">Thus the leading terms control both components. This calculation makes
explicit the role of the corrector in the modified <math id="A2.SS3.p5.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> hypocoercivity
argument; see also Fan, Li, and Lu <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We now turn from the idealized calculation to the contraction proof. The
modified <math id="A2.SS3.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> argument has two steps: we first show that the Lyapunov
function is equivalent to the squared <math id="A2.SS3.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> norm and then establish its
one-step decay.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.3</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Equivalence with the squared <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> norm)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\omega\leq\gamma_{\rm gap}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ω</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\omega\leq\gamma_{\rm gap}</annotation></semantics></math>, then every
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in L_{0}^{2}(\pi_{\eta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in L_{0}^{2}(\pi_{\eta})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A2.E22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}\,\|f\|^{2}\leq\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(f)\leq\frac{3}{2}\,\|f\|^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℒ</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}\,\|f\|^{2}\leq\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(f)\leq\frac{3}{2}\,\|f\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">The operators <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> commute, so
<math id="A2.SS3.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is self-adjoint on
<math id="A2.SS3.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="I+(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1})^{2}=I+\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-2}=\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-2}\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">I+(\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1})^{2}=I+\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-2}=\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-2}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">where the last identity uses <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2}+\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{2}=I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2}+\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{2}=I</annotation></semantics></math>.
By (<a href="#A2.E20" title="Equation B.20 ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.20</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex20"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 2\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 2\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex20.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Bigl\langle\begin{pmatrix}f_{\mathsf{P}}\\
f_{\mathsf{V}}\end{pmatrix}\,,\begin{pmatrix}I&amp;-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\\
-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}&amp;-I\end{pmatrix}\begin{pmatrix}f_{\mathsf{P}}\\
f_{\mathsf{V}}\end{pmatrix}\Bigr\rangle\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>I</mi></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Bigl\langle\begin{pmatrix}f_{\mathsf{P}}\\
f_{\mathsf{V}}\end{pmatrix}\,,\begin{pmatrix}I&amp;-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\\
-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}&amp;-I\end{pmatrix}\begin{pmatrix}f_{\mathsf{P}}\\
f_{\mathsf{V}}\end{pmatrix}\Bigr\rangle\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">The square of the block operator in this display is</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{pmatrix}I&amp;-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\\
-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}&amp;-I\end{pmatrix}^{\!2}=\begin{pmatrix}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-2}&amp;0\\
0&amp;\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-2}\end{pmatrix}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>I</mi></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mtd><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd><mtd><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{pmatrix}I&amp;-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\\
-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}&amp;-I\end{pmatrix}^{\!2}=\begin{pmatrix}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-2}&amp;0\\
0&amp;\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-2}\end{pmatrix}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">Since the block operator is self-adjoint and
<math id="A2.SS3.p7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\succeq\gamma_{\rm gap}I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\succeq\gamma_{\rm gap}I</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Bigl\|\begin{pmatrix}I&amp;-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\\
-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}&amp;-I\end{pmatrix}\Bigr\|=\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\|\leq\frac{1}{\gamma_{\rm gap}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><mi>I</mi></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Bigl\|\begin{pmatrix}I&amp;-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\\
-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}&amp;-I\end{pmatrix}\Bigr\|=\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\|\leq\frac{1}{\gamma_{\rm gap}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p7.5.1" class="ltx_text">Applying this operator norm bound to the preceding quadratic form gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.E23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})|\leq\frac{1}{2\gamma_{\rm gap}}\,\bigl(\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}\bigr)\leq\frac{1}{2\gamma_{\rm gap}}\,\|f\|^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})|\leq\frac{1}{2\gamma_{\rm gap}}\,\bigl(\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}\bigr)\leq\frac{1}{2\gamma_{\rm gap}}\,\|f\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p7.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p7.6.1" class="ltx_text">Here the second inequality uses <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}\leq\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}=\|f\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}\leq\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}=\|f\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Finally, (<a href="#A2.E19" title="Equation B.19 ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.19</span></a>),
(<a href="#A2.E23" title="Equation B.23 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.23</span></a>), and <math id="A2.SS3.p7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega\leq\gamma_{\rm gap}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega\leq\gamma_{\rm gap}</annotation></semantics></math> imply</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bigl|\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(f)-\|f\|^{2}\bigr|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℒ</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bigl|\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(f)-\|f\|^{2}\bigr|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E24.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\omega\,|\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})|\leq\frac{\omega}{2\gamma_{\rm gap}}\,\|f\|^{2}\leq\frac{1}{2}\,\|f\|^{2}\,.\qed" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ω</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">.</mo><mo class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" lspace="0.0835em" mathvariant="italic" separator="true">∎</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\omega\,|\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})|\leq\frac{\omega}{2\gamma_{\rm gap}}\,\|f\|^{2}\leq\frac{1}{2}\,\|f\|^{2}\,.\qed</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.4</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(One-step decay of the Lyapunov function)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">There exist universal constants <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\rm hyp},c_{0},c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>hyp</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\rm hyp},c_{0},c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> such that the
following holds. Set</span></p>
<table id="A2.E25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\rho}\coloneqq\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})+\Bigl(\frac{\rho}{\gamma_{\rm gap}}\Bigr)^{2}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\omega\coloneqq\frac{c_{\rm hyp}\rho}{\Lambda_{\rho}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>≔</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>hyp</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\rho}\coloneqq\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})+\Bigl(\frac{\rho}{\gamma_{\rm gap}}\Bigr)^{2}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\omega\coloneqq\frac{c_{\rm hyp}\rho}{\Lambda_{\rho}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.25)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta\eta\leq c_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta\eta\leq c_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, then every
<math id="A2.Thmtheorem4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in L_{0}^{2}(\pi_{\eta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in L_{0}^{2}(\pi_{\eta})</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A2.E26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(\mathsf{K}f)\leq\Bigl(1-\frac{c\rho}{\Lambda_{\rho}}\Bigr)\,\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(f)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℒ</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℒ</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(\mathsf{K}f)\leq\Bigl(1-\frac{c\rho}{\Lambda_{\rho}}\Bigr)\,\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(f)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.26)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Take <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0}\leq 1/16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}\leq 1/16</annotation></semantics></math>. Then
<math id="A2.SS3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\rm gap}\leq 2\sqrt{\alpha\eta}\leq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\rm gap}\leq 2\sqrt{\alpha\eta}\leq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>, and consequently
<math id="A2.SS3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\rho}\geq\log 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\rho}\geq\log 2</annotation></semantics></math>.
We compare the actual update with the idealized operator analyzed above.
Let <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g\coloneqq\mathsf{K}_{\rm id}f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mi>id</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g\coloneqq\mathsf{K}_{\rm id}f</annotation></semantics></math>,
<math id="A2.SS3.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\mathsf{P}}\coloneqq\mathsf{P}g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\mathsf{P}}\coloneqq\mathsf{P}g</annotation></semantics></math>, and
<math id="A2.SS3.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\mathsf{V}}\coloneqq\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{P}^{\perp}g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\mathsf{V}}\coloneqq\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{P}^{\perp}g</annotation></semantics></math>.
By the definitions of <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝖪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{K}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{K}_{\rm id}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mi>id</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{K}_{\rm id}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex23"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{K}f-\mathsf{K}_{\rm id}f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mi>id</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{K}f-\mathsf{K}_{\rm id}f</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex23.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathsf{U}\bigl[I+(1-\rho)\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}\bigr]f_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathsf{U}\bigl[I+(1-\rho)\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}\bigr]f_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex24"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathsf{U}\bigl[\rho f_{\perp}+(1-\rho)(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})f_{\perp}\bigr]\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝖴</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathsf{U}\bigl[\rho f_{\perp}+(1-\rho)(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})f_{\perp}\bigr]\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Using <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}=\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}=\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS3.p8.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\perp}=-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{U}_{\perp\perp}=-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, the two components of
this difference are</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex25"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{P}(\mathsf{K}f-\mathsf{K}_{\rm id}f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mi>id</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{P}(\mathsf{K}f-\mathsf{K}_{\rm id}f)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex25.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\bigl[I+(1-\rho)\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}\bigr]f_{\perp}\,," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\bigl[I+(1-\rho)\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}\bigr]f_{\perp}\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex26"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{P}^{\perp}(\mathsf{K}f-\mathsf{K}_{\rm id}f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mi>id</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\mathsf{P}^{\perp}(\mathsf{K}f-\mathsf{K}_{\rm id}f)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\bigl[I+(1-\rho)\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}\bigr]f_{\perp}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\bigl[I+(1-\rho)\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}\bigr]f_{\perp}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">The same vector therefore determines both components of the error. Denote
it by</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\rho}\coloneqq\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\bigl[I+(1-\rho)\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}\bigr]f_{\perp}=\rho f_{\mathsf{V}}+(1-\rho)r\,,\hskip 20.00003ptr\coloneqq\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})f_{\perp}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\rho}\coloneqq\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}\bigl[I+(1-\rho)\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}\bigr]f_{\perp}=\rho f_{\mathsf{V}}+(1-\rho)r\,,\hskip 20.00003ptr\coloneqq\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})f_{\perp}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">Both <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math> belong to <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mrow><mi>𝖯</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathfrak{H}_{\mathsf{P},0}</annotation></semantics></math>. In
<math id="A2.SS3.p8.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>, the first
term comes from refreshment, while the second measures the departure of
the half turn from <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-I_{\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><msub><mi>ℌ</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-I_{\mathfrak{H}_{\perp}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Consequently,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{P}}=g_{\mathsf{P}}+\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt(\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{V}}=g_{\mathsf{V}}-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{P}}=g_{\mathsf{P}}+\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\,,\hskip 20.00003pt(\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{V}}=g_{\mathsf{V}}-\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.27)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p8.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p8.5.1" class="ltx_text">Substituting (<a href="#A2.E27" title="Equation B.27 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.27</span></a>) into the definition
(<a href="#A2.E20" title="Equation B.20 ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.20</span></a>) of the corrector <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{C}</annotation></semantics></math> and expanding
gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathscr{C}\bigl((\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{P}},(\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{V}}\bigr)-\mathscr{C}(g_{\mathsf{P}},g_{\mathsf{V}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathscr{C}\bigl((\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{P}},(\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{V}}\bigr)-\mathscr{C}(g_{\mathsf{P}},g_{\mathsf{V}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 20.00003pt=\bigl\langle g_{\mathsf{P}},\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle+\bigl\langle g_{\mathsf{V}},\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle+\frac{1}{2}\,\bigl(\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\|^{2}-\|\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\|^{2}\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 20.00003pt=\bigl\langle g_{\mathsf{P}},\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle+\bigl\langle g_{\mathsf{V}},\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle+\frac{1}{2}\,\bigl(\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\|^{2}-\|\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\|^{2}\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 20.00003pt\hskip 20.00003pt+{}\bigl\langle\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}g_{\mathsf{P}},\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle-\bigl\langle\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho},g_{\mathsf{V}}\bigr\rangle+\|\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 20.00003pt\hskip 20.00003pt+{}\bigl\langle\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}g_{\mathsf{P}},\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle-\bigl\langle\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho},g_{\mathsf{V}}\bigr\rangle+\|\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex31"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 20.00003pt=\bigl\langle g_{\mathsf{P}},\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle+\bigl\langle\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}g_{\mathsf{P}},\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle+\frac{1}{2}\,\bigl(\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\|^{2}+\|\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\|^{2}\bigr)\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 20.00003pt=\bigl\langle g_{\mathsf{P}},\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle+\bigl\langle\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}g_{\mathsf{P}},\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle+\frac{1}{2}\,\bigl(\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\|^{2}+\|\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\|^{2}\bigr)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p8.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p8.6.1" class="ltx_text">In the last equality, the two terms containing <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\mathsf{V}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\mathsf{V}}</annotation></semantics></math> cancel.
For the terms linear in <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the commutation of
<math id="A2.SS3.p8.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}</annotation></semantics></math> and the identity
<math id="A2.SS3.p8.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2}+\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{2}=I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2}+\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{2}=I</annotation></semantics></math> give</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex32"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bigl\langle g_{\mathsf{P}},\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle+\bigl\langle\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}g_{\mathsf{P}},\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bigl\langle g_{\mathsf{P}},\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle+\bigl\langle\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}g_{\mathsf{P}},\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex33"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 20.00003pt=\bigl\langle g_{\mathsf{P}},(\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}+\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2})r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle=\bigl\langle g_{\mathsf{P}},\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="2.278em">=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 20.00003pt=\bigl\langle g_{\mathsf{P}},(\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}+\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}^{2})r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle=\bigl\langle g_{\mathsf{P}},\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p8.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p8.7.1" class="ltx_text">The same identity reduces the quadratic terms to</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}\,\bigl(\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\|^{2}+\|\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\|^{2}\bigr)=\frac{1}{2}\,\|r_{\rho}\|^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝖴</mi><mi>𝖯𝖯</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}\,\bigl(\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\|^{2}+\|\mathsf{U}_{\mathsf{P}\mathsf{P}}r_{\rho}\|^{2}\bigr)=\frac{1}{2}\,\|r_{\rho}\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p8.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p8.8.1" class="ltx_text">Consequently, combined with (<a href="#A2.E21" title="Equation B.21 ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.21</span></a>),</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex35"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathscr{C}\bigl((\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{P}},(\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{V}}\bigr)-\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathscr{C}\bigl((\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{P}},(\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{V}}\bigr)-\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex36"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 10.00002pt=\bigl[\mathscr{C}\bigl((\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{P}},(\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{V}}\bigr)-\mathscr{C}(g_{\mathsf{P}},g_{\mathsf{V}})\bigr]+\bigl[\mathscr{C}(g_{\mathsf{P}},g_{\mathsf{V}})-\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})\bigr]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="1.278em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 10.00002pt=\bigl[\mathscr{C}\bigl((\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{P}},(\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{V}}\bigr)-\mathscr{C}(g_{\mathsf{P}},g_{\mathsf{V}})\bigr]+\bigl[\mathscr{C}(g_{\mathsf{P}},g_{\mathsf{V}})-\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})\bigr]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.E28"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 10.00002pt=-\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}+\bigl\langle g_{\mathsf{P}},\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle+\frac{1}{2}\,\|r_{\rho}\|^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo lspace="1.278em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 10.00002pt=-\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}+\bigl\langle g_{\mathsf{P}},\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle+\frac{1}{2}\,\|r_{\rho}\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.28)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p8.9" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p8.9.1" class="ltx_text">Thus, it remains to estimate <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r_{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r_{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{L}\coloneqq(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝖫</mi><mo>≔</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{L}\coloneqq(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p8.10" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p8.10.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=\mathsf{L}^{*}f_{\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝖫</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=\mathsf{L}^{*}f_{\perp}</annotation></semantics></math>, applying
(<a href="#A2.E17" title="Equation B.17 ‣ Proposition B.2 (Global half-turn bound). ‣ B.2 Estimates for the reflection and half-turn operators ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.17</span></a>) to <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}v" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}v</annotation></semantics></math> and then taking
adjoints gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E29"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}r\|^{2}=\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})f_{\perp}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}r\|^{2}=\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}(I+\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp})f_{\perp}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq C\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq C\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.29)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p8.11" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p8.11.1" class="ltx_text">Together with <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\succeq\gamma_{\rm gap}I" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>⪰</mo><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}\succeq\gamma_{\rm gap}I</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS3.p8.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|\leq\|f_{\perp}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|\leq\|f_{\perp}\|</annotation></semantics></math>, this gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.E30"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}r_{\rho}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}r_{\rho}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E30.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\rho^{2}\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}f_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}+2(1-\rho)^{2}\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}r\|^{2}\leq C\Lambda_{\rho}\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ρ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\rho^{2}\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}f_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}+2(1-\rho)^{2}\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}r\|^{2}\leq C\Lambda_{\rho}\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.30)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p8.12" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p8.12.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, since <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝖵</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>⟂</mo><mi>𝖯</mi></mrow><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{V}_{\perp\mathsf{P}}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖧</mi><mrow><mo>⟂</mo><mo lspace="0em">⁣</mo><mo>⟂</mo></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{H}_{\perp\perp}</annotation></semantics></math> are contractions, <math id="A2.SS3.p8.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|r_{\rho}\|\leq\rho\,\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|+(1-\rho)\,\|r\|\leq 2\,\|f_{\perp}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|r_{\rho}\|\leq\rho\,\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|+(1-\rho)\,\|r\|\leq 2\,\|f_{\perp}\|</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p9.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p9.2.1" class="ltx_text">The rotation formula for <math id="A2.SS3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{K}_{\rm id}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝖪</mi><mi>id</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{K}_{\rm id}</annotation></semantics></math> gives <math id="A2.SS3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|g_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}\leq\|g_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\|g_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}=\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|g_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}\leq\|g_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\|g_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}=\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Hence, Young’s inequality and
(<a href="#A2.E30" title="Equation B.30 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.30</span></a>) give</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex38"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\bigl|\bigl\langle g_{\mathsf{P}},\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle\bigr|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" stretchy="true">⟩</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\bigl|\bigl\langle g_{\mathsf{P}},\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}r_{\rho}\bigr\rangle\bigr|</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex38.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{4}\,\|g_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+C\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}r_{\rho}\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_mathvariant_sans-serif" mathvariant="sans-serif">Γ</mi><mi>𝖯</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>r</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{4}\,\|g_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+C\,\|\mathsf{\Gamma}_{\mathsf{P}}^{-1}r_{\rho}\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{4}\,\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\frac{1}{4}\,\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}+C\Lambda_{\rho}\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\frac{1}{4}\,\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\frac{1}{4}\,\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|^{2}+C\Lambda_{\rho}\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p9.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p9.3.1" class="ltx_text">Inserting these estimates into
(<a href="#A2.E28" title="Equation B.28 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.28</span></a>), and using
<math id="A2.SS3.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|\leq\|f_{\perp}\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f_{\mathsf{V}}\|\leq\|f_{\perp}\|</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS3.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\rho}\geq\log 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\rho}\geq\log 2</annotation></semantics></math>, gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.E31" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E31X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E31X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathscr{C}\bigl((\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{P}},(\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{V}}\bigr)-\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})\leq-\frac{1}{2}\,\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+C\Lambda_{\rho}\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">𝒞</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖵</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathscr{C}\bigl((\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{P}},(\mathsf{K}f)_{\mathsf{V}}\bigr)-\mathscr{C}(f_{\mathsf{P}},f_{\mathsf{V}})\leq-\frac{1}{2}\,\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+C\Lambda_{\rho}\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(B.31)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Finally, (<a href="#A2.E18" title="Equation B.18 ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.18</span></a>) and
(<a href="#A2.E31" title="Equation B.31 ‣ Proof. ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.31</span></a>) give</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(\mathsf{K}f)-\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℒ</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℒ</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(\mathsf{K}f)-\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(f)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex40.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq-\rho\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}+\frac{c_{\rm hyp}\rho}{\Lambda_{\rho}}\,\Bigl(-\frac{1}{2}\,\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+C\Lambda_{\rho}\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\Bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>hyp</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq-\rho\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}+\frac{c_{\rm hyp}\rho}{\Lambda_{\rho}}\,\Bigl(-\frac{1}{2}\,\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+C\Lambda_{\rho}\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\Bigr)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\frac{c_{\rm hyp}\rho}{2\Lambda_{\rho}}\,\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}-(1-Cc_{\rm hyp})\,\rho\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>hyp</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>hyp</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\frac{c_{\rm hyp}\rho}{2\Lambda_{\rho}}\,\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}-(1-Cc_{\rm hyp})\,\rho\,\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p10.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p10.2.1" class="ltx_text">Choose <math id="A2.SS3.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{\rm hyp}\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>hyp</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{\rm hyp}\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> sufficiently small so that
<math id="A2.SS3.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Cc_{\rm hyp}\leq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>hyp</mi></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Cc_{\rm hyp}\leq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>. Since <math id="A2.SS3.p10.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\rho}\geq\log 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\rho}\geq\log 2</annotation></semantics></math>, the last display is
then bounded above by</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex42" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\frac{c\rho}{\Lambda_{\rho}}\,\bigl(\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\bigr)=-\frac{c\rho}{\Lambda_{\rho}}\,\|f\|^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>𝖯</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mo>⟂</mo></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\frac{c\rho}{\Lambda_{\rho}}\,\bigl(\|f_{\mathsf{P}}\|^{2}+\|f_{\perp}\|^{2}\bigr)=-\frac{c\rho}{\Lambda_{\rho}}\,\|f\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p10.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p10.3.1" class="ltx_text">It remains to compare the last norm with the Lyapunov function. The
elementary inequality <math id="A2.SS3.p10.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x/(a+x^{2})\leq 1/(2\sqrt{a})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mi>a</mi></msqrt></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x/(a+x^{2})\leq 1/(2\sqrt{a})</annotation></semantics></math>, for <math id="A2.SS3.p10.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS3.p10.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\omega}{\gamma_{\rm gap}}=c_{\rm hyp}\,\frac{\rho/\gamma_{\rm gap}}{\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})+(\rho/\gamma_{\rm gap})^{2}}\leq\frac{c_{\rm hyp}}{2\sqrt{\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})}}\leq\frac{c_{\rm hyp}}{2\sqrt{\log 2}}\leq 1\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mi>ω</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>hyp</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>hyp</mi></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>hyp</mi></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\omega}{\gamma_{\rm gap}}=c_{\rm hyp}\,\frac{\rho/\gamma_{\rm gap}}{\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})+(\rho/\gamma_{\rm gap})^{2}}\leq\frac{c_{\rm hyp}}{2\sqrt{\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})}}\leq\frac{c_{\rm hyp}}{2\sqrt{\log 2}}\leq 1\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p10.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p10.4.1" class="ltx_text">Thus <math id="A2.SS3.p10.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega\leq\gamma_{\rm gap}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ω</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega\leq\gamma_{\rm gap}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the upper bound in
<a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma B.3 (Equivalence with the squared 𝐿^2 norm). ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a> gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex44" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex44.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|f\|^{2}\geq\frac{2}{3}\,\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(f)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℒ</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|f\|^{2}\geq\frac{2}{3}\,\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(f)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p10.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p10.5.1" class="ltx_text">Consequently,</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(\mathsf{K}f)\leq\Bigl(1-\frac{2c\rho}{3\Lambda_{\rho}}\Bigr)\,\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(f)\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℒ</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝖪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℒ</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(\mathsf{K}f)\leq\Bigl(1-\frac{2c\rho}{3\Lambda_{\rho}}\Bigr)\,\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(f)\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p10.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p10.6.1" class="ltx_text">which is (<a href="#A2.E26" title="Equation B.26 ‣ Lemma B.4 (One-step decay of the Lyapunov function). ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.26</span></a>) after renaming the universal
constant.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p11" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p11.1" class="ltx_p">Combining
<a href="#A2.Thmtheorem3" title="Lemma B.3 (Equivalence with the squared 𝐿^2 norm). ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemmas</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a> and <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma B.4 (One-step decay of the Lyapunov function). ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>, we can now
prove the <math id="A2.SS3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> contraction in <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 3.5 (𝜒^2 convergence). ‣ 3.3 Ideal Proximal BPS ‣ 3 The Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof of <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem5" title="Theorem 3.5 (𝜒^2 convergence). ‣ 3.3 Ideal Proximal BPS ‣ 3 The Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Theorem</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.5</span></a>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS3.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">We first turn the one-step Lyapunov decay into a fixed <math id="A2.SS3.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> contraction
over a block of <math id="A2.SS3.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> steps, and then apply this contraction to densities.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p13" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">Take <math id="A2.SS3.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> from <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma B.4 (One-step decay of the Lyapunov function). ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a> and choose a fixed
universal <math id="A2.SS3.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{\star}\in(0,1/2]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{\star}\in(0,1/2]</annotation></semantics></math>. The one-step estimate requires
<math id="A2.SS3.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\leq 1/2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\leq 1/2</annotation></semantics></math>. Since
<math id="A2.SS3.p13.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\eta\leq\beta\eta\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\eta\leq\beta\eta\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS3.p13.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\log(e/x)\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\log(e/x)\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A2.SS3.p13.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;x\leq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;x\leq 1</annotation></semantics></math>, the prescribed refreshment
probability satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0&lt;\rho=\rho_{\star}\sqrt{\alpha\eta\log\frac{e}{\alpha\eta}}\leq\rho_{\star}\leq\frac{1}{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mfrac><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0&lt;\rho=\rho_{\star}\sqrt{\alpha\eta\log\frac{e}{\alpha\eta}}\leq\rho_{\star}\leq\frac{1}{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS3.p14" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">The decay rate in <a href="#A2.Thmtheorem4" title="Lemma B.4 (One-step decay of the Lyapunov function). ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Lemma</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a> is
<math id="A2.SS3.p14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho/\Lambda_{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>/</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho/\Lambda_{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math>, so a fixed contraction is obtained by taking
<math id="A2.SS3.p14.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> proportional to <math id="A2.SS3.p14.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\rho}/\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\rho}/\rho</annotation></semantics></math>. We first bound this ratio.
Recall that
<math id="A2.SS3.p14.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma_{\rm gap}\asymp\sqrt{\alpha\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub><mo>≍</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma_{\rm gap}\asymp\sqrt{\alpha\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS3.p14.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})\asymp\log(e/(\alpha\eta))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≍</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})\asymp\log(e/(\alpha\eta))</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex47" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex47.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Bigl(\frac{\rho}{\gamma_{\rm gap}}\Bigr)^{2}\leq C\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\rho\geq c\gamma_{\rm gap}\sqrt{\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mfrac><mi>ρ</mi><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Bigl(\frac{\rho}{\gamma_{\rm gap}}\Bigr)^{2}\leq C\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})\,,\hskip 20.00003pt\rho\geq c\gamma_{\rm gap}\sqrt{\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">It follows from the definition of <math id="A2.SS3.p14.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math> that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex48"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\Lambda_{\rho}}{\rho}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mi>ρ</mi></mfrac></mstyle><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\Lambda_{\rho}}{\rho}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex48.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq C\,\frac{\sqrt{\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})}}{\gamma_{\rm gap}}\leq\frac{C}{\sqrt{\alpha\eta}}\sqrt{\log\frac{e}{\alpha\eta}}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msqrt><msub><mi>γ</mi><mi>gap</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>C</mi><msqrt><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>e</mi><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>η</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq C\,\frac{\sqrt{\log(1/\gamma_{\rm gap})}}{\gamma_{\rm gap}}\leq\frac{C}{\sqrt{\alpha\eta}}\sqrt{\log\frac{e}{\alpha\eta}}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p14.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p14.3.1" class="ltx_text">Choose a sufficiently large universal constant <math id="A2.SS3.p14.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and consider</span></p>
<table id="A2.E32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq C_{1}\,\frac{\Lambda_{\rho}}{\rho}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mi>ρ</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq C_{1}\,\frac{\Lambda_{\rho}}{\rho}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.32)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p14.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p14.4.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A2.SS3.p14.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in L_{0}^{2}(\pi_{\eta})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mn>0</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in L_{0}^{2}(\pi_{\eta})</annotation></semantics></math>, take <math id="A2.SS3.p14.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\omega</annotation></semantics></math> as in
(<a href="#A2.E25" title="Equation B.25 ‣ Lemma B.4 (One-step decay of the Lyapunov function). ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.25</span></a>). Iterating
(<a href="#A2.E26" title="Equation B.26 ‣ Lemma B.4 (One-step decay of the Lyapunov function). ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.26</span></a>) over this block gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(\mathsf{K}^{N}f)\leq\Bigl(1-\frac{c\rho}{\Lambda_{\rho}}\Bigr)^{N}\,\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(f)\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℒ</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝖪</mi><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℒ</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.150em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(\mathsf{K}^{N}f)\leq\Bigl(1-\frac{c\rho}{\Lambda_{\rho}}\Bigr)^{N}\,\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(f)\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p14.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p14.5.1" class="ltx_text">Applying the lower bound in (<a href="#A2.E22" title="Equation B.22 ‣ Lemma B.3 (Equivalence with the squared 𝐿^2 norm). ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.22</span></a>) to
<math id="A2.SS3.p14.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathsf{K}^{N}f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝖪</mi><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathsf{K}^{N}f</annotation></semantics></math> and the upper bound to <math id="A2.SS3.p14.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex50"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\mathsf{K}^{N}f\|^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝖪</mi><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\mathsf{K}^{N}f\|^{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex50.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq 2\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(\mathsf{K}^{N}f)\leq 2\,\Bigl(1-\frac{c\rho}{\Lambda_{\rho}}\Bigr)^{N}\,\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(f)\leq 3\,\Bigl(1-\frac{c\rho}{\Lambda_{\rho}}\Bigr)^{N}\,\|f\|^{2}\leq 3e^{-cC_{1}}\,\|f\|^{2}\,." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℒ</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝖪</mi><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathscript">ℒ</mi><mi>ω</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.150em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq 2\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(\mathsf{K}^{N}f)\leq 2\,\Bigl(1-\frac{c\rho}{\Lambda_{\rho}}\Bigr)^{N}\,\mathscr{L}_{\omega}(f)\leq 3\,\Bigl(1-\frac{c\rho}{\Lambda_{\rho}}\Bigr)^{N}\,\|f\|^{2}\leq 3e^{-cC_{1}}\,\|f\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p14.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p14.6.1" class="ltx_text">The last step uses <math id="A2.SS3.p14.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-x\leq e^{-x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-x\leq e^{-x}</annotation></semantics></math> and
<math id="A2.SS3.p14.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N\geq C_{1}\Lambda_{\rho}/\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N\geq C_{1}\Lambda_{\rho}/\rho</annotation></semantics></math>.
Taking <math id="A2.SS3.p14.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> sufficiently large makes <math id="A2.SS3.p14.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3e^{-cC_{1}}\leq e^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3e^{-cC_{1}}\leq e^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math>. Thus,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E33.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathsf{K}^{N}f\|^{2}\leq e^{-1}\,\|f\|^{2}\,." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝖪</mi><mi>N</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathsf{K}^{N}f\|^{2}\leq e^{-1}\,\|f\|^{2}\,.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(B.33)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p14.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p14.7.1" class="ltx_text">Iterating by blocks, the <math id="A2.SS3.p14.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{2}</annotation></semantics></math> contraction
(<a href="#A2.E33" title="Equation B.33 ‣ Proof of . ‣ B.3 Modified 𝐿^2 contraction and proof of the main theorem ‣ Appendix B Operator formulation and modified 𝐿^2 contraction ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.33</span></a>) is equivalently, by (<a href="#A4.E5" title="Equation D.5 ‣ D.1 Hilbert space and Markov operator conventions ‣ Appendix D Technical tools ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.5</span></a>) and the
adjoint remark following it, the <math id="A2.SS3.p14.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\chi^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>-estimate</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\chi^{2}\bigl(\nu_{0}\mathcal{K}^{JN}\|\pi_{\eta}\bigr)\leq e^{-J}\chi^{2}(\nu_{0}\|\pi_{\eta})\,," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒦</mi><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>J</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mi>χ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ν</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.150em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\chi^{2}\bigl(\nu_{0}\mathcal{K}^{JN}\|\pi_{\eta}\bigr)\leq e^{-J}\chi^{2}(\nu_{0}\|\pi_{\eta})\,,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS3.p14.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.p14.8.1" class="ltx_text">which proves (<a href="#S3.E14" title="Equation 3.14 ‣ Theorem 3.5 (𝜒^2 convergence). ‣ 3.3 Ideal Proximal BPS ‣ 3 The Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.14</span></a>). The <math id="A2.SS3.p14.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>X</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X</annotation></semantics></math>-marginal of
<math id="A2.SS3.p14.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\eta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>η</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\eta}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A2.SS3.p14.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math>, and total variation cannot increase under
projection. Moreover, Cauchy–Schwarz gives
<math id="A2.SS3.p14.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{TV}(P,Q)\leq\tfrac{1}{2}\sqrt{\chi^{2}(P\|Q)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>TV</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>χ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{TV}(P,Q)\leq\tfrac{1}{2}\sqrt{\chi^{2}(P\|Q)}</annotation></semantics></math>, which gives (<a href="#S3.E15" title="Equation 3.15 ‣ Theorem 3.5 (𝜒^2 convergence). ‣ 3.3 Ideal Proximal BPS ‣ 3 The Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler ‣ Accelerated High-Accuracy Sampling from a Warm Startvia the Proximal Bouncy Particle Sampler" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.15</span></a>).
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>